From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 23:50:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ppc32: fix MulHigh32/MulHighU32 - do not use 64-bit clrldi

kPPC_MulHigh32 and kPPC_MulHighU32 clear the (undefined) upper 32 bits
of the 64-bit result register with clrldi, which only exists on ppc64
(assembler declares it under V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64), breaking the ppc32
compile. On 32-bit there are no upper bits to clear: mulhw/mulhwu leave
exactly the high 32-bit word in the destination, so emit them directly
into the output register.

These were the only unguarded uses of 64-bit-only assembler mnemonics
in 32-bit-compiled code across the whole ppc backend (codegen,
compiler/backend, builtins, deoptimizer, debug, regexp, liftoff).
---
 deps/v8/src/compiler/backend/ppc/code-generator-ppc.cc | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

--- a/deps/v8/src/compiler/backend/ppc/code-generator-ppc.cc
+++ b/deps/v8/src/compiler/backend/ppc/code-generator-ppc.cc
@@ -1525,14 +1525,24 @@
       }
       break;
     case kPPC_MulHigh32:
+#if V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64
       __ mulhw(r0, i.InputRegister(0), i.InputRegister(1), i.OutputRCBit());
       // High 32 bits are undefined and need to be cleared.
       __ clrldi(i.OutputRegister(), r0, Operand(32));
+#else
+      __ mulhw(i.OutputRegister(), i.InputRegister(0), i.InputRegister(1),
+               i.OutputRCBit());
+#endif
       break;
     case kPPC_MulHighU32:
+#if V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64
       __ mulhwu(r0, i.InputRegister(0), i.InputRegister(1), i.OutputRCBit());
       // High 32 bits are undefined and need to be cleared.
       __ clrldi(i.OutputRegister(), r0, Operand(32));
+#else
+      __ mulhwu(i.OutputRegister(), i.InputRegister(0), i.InputRegister(1),
+                i.OutputRCBit());
+#endif
       break;
     case kPPC_MulDouble:
       ASSEMBLE_FLOAT_BINOP_RC(fmul, MiscField::decode(instr->opcode()));
-- 
